      "writtenOn": "2022-07-14T19:11:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I added a runtime flag for this within this CL. The \u0027child\u0027 CL to this one adds a runtime flag to split up tracing sessions/files by nanobench benchmark, so I added a TODO to explicate how that naming convention will work once that flag is added.\n\nFor example, if they elect to split up files by benchmark, the files currently get saved under the desired user-entered output path and file extension, but the file name is that of the current benchmark (not the base file name that the user passed in). Does that seem appropriate? The other option would be to use the base file name the user passes in, but append escalating numbers to it as more tracing sessions/files are created, but this seems less intuitive to me.",
