        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-14T19:11:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I can see how this doesn\u0027t make much sense without the context of the subsequent CL. See my reply to your previous comment (#93, https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/548398/7/tools/trace/SkPerfettoTrace.cpp#93) and my new comment within the code that I added above this assignment for an explanation as to why we store the base output file name within the class itself.\n\nTL;DR: I store the different file name components separately (and solicit the components from the user using separate runtime flags) so that if they elect to split the tracing session by benchmark, we can use their desired output path and file extension while selecting a unique base file name for each benchmark / tracing session. I store the base file name as a member variable because we need access to it when closing the current tracing session, which is called from the argument-less destructor of the class.\n\nPlease let me know if you have an idea of a better way to go about this.",
      "parentUuid": "8f4e40ac_b7cea612",
      "range": {
